# Native Android Multi-Module Navigation

Canonical pattern: `:app` root graph, `feature/*/presentation/navigation/`, `core/common/navigation/AppRoutes.kt`.

> Native Android only. Library: `androidx.navigation:navigation-compose`.

## Ownership

| Layer | Owns navigation |
|-------|-----------------|
| `:app` | Single `NavHostController`, root `AppNavGraph`, top-level tabs, deep-link entry |
| `:feature/*` | Routes, NavCallbacks, nested graph, screen registrations |
| `:core:common` | `AppRoutes` marker only — no NavHost, no feature imports |
| `:core:designsystem` | Bottom bar / rail UI — not routing logic |
| `:shared/*` | **No navigation** — business domain only |

**Golden rule:** Only `:app` creates `NavHostController` and maps callbacks across features.

```
app → feature → shared → core
```

- Features **never** depend on other features for navigation
- Cross-feature targets resolve only in `app/.../AppNavGraph.kt`
- Do not register `NavHostController` in Hilt/Koin — keep it in composable scope

## Three files per feature graph

```
feature/<name>/presentation/navigation/
├── {Feature}Routes.kt       # @Serializable typed destinations
├── {Feature}NavCallbacks.kt # sealed navigation intents (not serializable)
└── {Feature}NavGraph.kt     # NavGraphBuilder.{feature}NavGraph()
```

```kotlin
fun NavGraphBuilder.homeScreen(
    modifier: Modifier,
    onNavRoute: (HomeNavCallbacks) -> Unit,
) {
    composable<HomeRoutes.HomeScreen> {
        // UI emits onNavRoute(...) — never navController.navigate()
    }
}
```

## Typed routes

- All destinations extend `AppRoutes` and use `@Serializable`
- Register with `composable<Route>()` / `navigation<GraphRoute>()`
- Read args: `backStackEntry.toRoute<Route>()`
- Serialization plugin required on modules that define routes

```kotlin
sealed class HomeRoutes : AppRoutes {
    @Serializable data object GraphRoute : HomeRoutes()
    @Serializable data object HomeScreen : HomeRoutes()
}
```

## Callback → navigate pattern

Features emit intents; `:app` performs navigation:

```kotlin
// feature — intent only
sealed interface HomeNavCallbacks {
    data object NavigateUp : HomeNavCallbacks
    sealed interface HomeScreen : HomeNavCallbacks {
        data object ToShop : HomeScreen
    }
}

// app/AppNavGraph.kt — single cross-feature router
homeNavGraph(onNavRoute = {
    when (it) {
        HomeNavCallbacks.NavigateUp -> navController.navigateUp()
        HomeNavCallbacks.HomeScreen.ToShop ->
            navController.navigateToTopLevel(TopLevelDestination.Shop)
    }
})
```

## Top-level tabs & flows

- Define `TopLevelDestination` in `:app` referencing feature `GraphRoute` / root screen
- Hide chrome on non-tab flows via `showsAppNavigation()`
- Exit multi-step flows with inclusive `popBackStack(route, inclusive = true)`
- Parse deep links in `MainActivity` / `:app` only — not ViewModels or `:shared/*`

## Anti-patterns

| ❌ Wrong | ✅ Correct |
|----------|-----------|
| `NavController` in ViewModel or feature | Callbacks from UI; navigate in `:app` |
| String-based routes | `@Serializable` typed routes |
| Feature → feature Gradle dep for nav | Route types imported by `:app` only |
| NavHost / AppNavGraph in `:shared/*` | Routing only in `:app` |
| Second NavHost outside app shell | One NavHost in `:app` |
| Auto-navigate on foreground push | Update UI in place; tap → deep link |

## Adding navigation checklist

1. Add `@Serializable` route(s) in `{Feature}Routes.kt`
2. Add intent(s) in `{Feature}NavCallbacks.kt`
3. Register screen in `NavGraphBuilder.{name}Screen()` extension
4. Wire graph in `{Feature}NavGraph.kt`
5. Register graph + `when` handler in `app/.../AppNavGraph.kt`
6. Cross-feature? Callback in source; target route in target feature — no feature-to-feature import
